## Glyph And Fidelity Notes

- 176 uses $b$, including both products and the two signed exponents; row 01 quantity is 7.
- 177 unit is 米/秒 and the source punctuation after the parenthesized unit instruction includes a final full stop.
- 178 is the historical estimate and forecast as printed, including two occurrences of 2000 and multiplier 37; do not update the temporal wording.
- БЭСМ-2 has visibly Cyrillic distinguishing letters. The second machine label has E- and C-shaped first letters, recorded here as Cyrillic ЕС-10-50. Latin EC and Cyrillic ЕС are genuinely indistinguishable as these printed glyphs; the pixels cannot settle a Unicode-codepoint difference. The actual visible designation includes both hyphens and numbers 10 and 50, not a single merged numeral. Preserve the printed glyphs and declare this script ambiguity rather than claiming pixel proof of the codepoints.
- 179 rate is $8\cdot10^3$, then $1.5\cdot10^6$; its two occurrences of 1975 are preserved.
- 180(б) explicitly has "2.6 分之一", across a line break, not a multiplier and not the fraction $2/6$.
- No other real unreadable/ambiguous text glyph identified. Margin flecks do not form source content.

